tside/inside wetness or exposure observations; a paid wet probe can test a reachable sample or roof section but does not certify the whole shelter. Record weather and measured result, including leaks. Wear each installed part each world round by 0.0005 + 0.002*rain + 0.002*wind; condition below 0.5 disables the affected bay until replacement and passing reinspection. Inspect costs one round and 0.2 energy. Builder repair costs exact replacement parts for the selected inherited stage, one round and one energy; replaced parts remain real worn ground materials. Builder dismantling costs one round and one energy per stage and returns only installed parts at current condition. Interruption preserves partial work and reservations; resume pays the next stage after revalidation. Cancel costs one round, zero energy, releases unused reservations once and leaves installed work unfinished. Death stops work, drops unused carried material at death and leaves installed parts on site. No spent time or energy is refunded. Ongoing wear continues during ordinary simulation, not development waiting. Implement these validations and exposure rules in code, with no repeated model adjudication.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":4,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"No benefit for requesting, naming, studying, registration or commissioning alone. Observable successful protection can produce personally applicable comfort, with total physical comfort capped at 10 and never reducing basic nutritional requirements. If the experience system supports it, actual protection during rain can give a short benefit capped at 1 per actor per 10 rounds; maintained satisfaction is capped at 1 for ongoing usable shelter access, refreshed only by actual use or maintenance and decaying at least 0.002 per round without qualifying activity. Functionally deduplicate across bays, shelter copies and equivalent comfort events. Genuine measured information gain, including a discovered leak or failed material test, may qualify once for that finding, not for repeated queries. Other users receive nothing unless they independently participate or experience the effect. Never modify protected rewards, budget, goals or permissions.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Emit observable events for material installation, stage interruption, inspection results, commissioning, leaks, repair, occupancy and dismantling. Reusable visual metadata must include structure ID, bay IDs, footprint, orientation, open approach, installed-stage mask, roof coverage, per-bay condition, commissioning status and actual occupant positions. Render partial frames and missing roof courses accurately; show protected occupancy only when runtime coverage and weather checks pass. Failed construction or tests must not display completed shelter or successful protection.\\\"},{\\\"actor\\\":\\\"wren\\\",\\\"decision\\\":\\\"develop\\\",\\\"ability\\\":null,\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Searches found probe, consult and exchange but no planting or cultivation operation. Probe can inspect or test a sample, not place viable propagules in a maintained growing site. Food safety and 14 nutrition do not establish root viability or growing requirements. Develop a general planting-and-tending trial with an executable observation-only outcome when regeneration remains unsupported, not instant replenishment or a fictional guaranteed crop.\\\",\\\"specification\\\":\\\"Handoff: implement 'Establish and tend a cultivation trial', parameterized by visible plant/source reference, exact owned propagule lot and quantity, reachable ground site, and mode establish/tend/observe/resume/cancel/remove. Reuse probe and consult for their actual supported operations and record those dependencies; use the existing plant lifecycle and resource-transfer handlers where compatible, without claiming them as new. Initial applicable references are source start-0-roots at (10.1,12), observed stock 2 and capacity 6, and owned lot item-4-wren-46, quantity 3 with existing age and decay. Revalidate all at execution; neither source stock nor ownership is frozen by this review. The owned food's edibility is not evidence of a living crown, bud or seed. First inspect a real candidate and reachable ground using probe: observation costs one round and 0.2 energy; physical testing costs one round, 0.5 energy and 0.1 actual material unit, preserving or consuming the sampled amount according to the performed test. Only observed evidence is reported. If no suitable living planting unit is established, leave the owned food untouched and allow a marked monitoring trial of the existing patch; do not invent a viable propagule. Minimal planting trial selects one actual whole viable unit, or a larger exact quantity when supported, and ground that can genuinely be loosened and covered by hand. No tool, water, fertilizer or seed is provided. Establishment has three one-round stages costing one energy each: prepare a small planting position appropriate to the actual propagule, place it, then cover and record. Site area, depth and suitability must come from observed propagule dimensions and applicable lifecycle requirements, not a universal guessed root depth. If the ground cannot be worked by hand, a real suitable tool or different workable site is required. Unplaced units remain reserved, owned and ageing; placement transfers the unit's quantity, provenance, mass and remaining viable state from inventory to the trial, not to food stock. Once planted it is unavailable to eat or plant elsewhere. Observation mode costs one round and 0.2 energy and records actual changes; tending costs one round and one energy per small trial plot, with an explicit supported action such as removing an observed competing plant by hand or restoring displaced soil. Irrigation requires actual accessible water, a feasible delivery method, exact quantity and paid collection/transport; it is not a free default action. Monitoring the existing patch need not remove its food or create a second plant. Runtime must bind to the real species' supported viability, moisture, light, soil, temperature and growth rules. Use the source's existing regeneration behavior if present; do not infer a rate from its stock/capacity or disclose hidden ecological parameters. If propagation is not yet modeled, implement establishment, environmental exposure, persistent trial records and comparison against the original patch as the feasible precursor, explicitly reporting that growth and yield are unverified. No autonomous food creation is enabled until a conserved, executable lifecycle is implemented in this same development handoff. Any enabled growth must advance only with elapsed simulation time and actual required environmental inputs; record growth inputs, viable biomass, stages, mortality and harvestable output. Never replenish by copying the planting unit or resetting the source. Harvest only observed mature stock through gather, debiting that stock at its existing costs. Preserve source food properties only where species identity remains established; nutrition is obtained through eating, not planting. Record elapsed rounds, placement stage, condition, observations and interventions. At 80 elapsed trial rounds offer an inconclusive status if no decisive change has occurred; this is an observation horizon, not a maturity deadline or unlock. Continued observation is optional. Real drought, waterlogging, decay, uprooting and inadequate conditions can stall or kill a trial. Growth and deterioration proceed during ordinary world simulation, not review waiting. Interruption preserves stage and reservations; resume rechecks site, energy and material validity and pays only subsequent work. Cancel costs one round and zero energy, releases unplaced survivors once, and leaves planted material in place. Removal costs one round and one energy and returns only the material actually recoverable in its current condition, never a guaranteed edible root. Death ends personal work, drops unplaced carried units and leaves the trial subject to ecology; independent actors may interact only through their own valid actions. Spent samples, labor and time are not refunded. Each learner studies individually for 2 rounds. Encode progress, accounting and failure rules rather than repeatedly asking a model to authorize growth.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":2,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"Requests, study, marking a plot and merely scheduling observations grant nothing. A verified new finding about viability, sprouting, failure or environmental response can support one bounded information-gain benefit, capped at 1 per actor per 10 rounds and deduplicated by finding across probe and trial interfaces. Familiar genuine tending or successful harvesting may sustain modest satisfaction without requiring novelty: cap at 1, refresh only on personally performed meaningful care or real harvest, and decay at least 0.002 per round without qualifying activity. Do not reward empty observations or repeated ineffective tending. A failed trial can be informative but cannot count as successful production. Physical comfort remains capped at 10; eating real harvested food retains its full basic nutrition independent of mood. No protected reward, budget, goal or permission changes.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Emit actual preparation, placement, tending, observation, emergence, wilting, death, removal and harvest events only when those events occur. Reusable metadata includes trial ID, source and lot references, site bounds, quantity placed, work stage, observation timestamps, measured condition, lifecycle stage and verified harvestable stock. Distinguish an observation marker from a planted unit and a planted unit from a sprout. Hidden roots remain visually hidden unless exposed by a real action. No lush crop, replenished stock, maturity indicator or successful-harvest animation may appear for an unverified, stalled or failed trial.\\\"}]}\"}","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}}

